%% Zero-downtime change of the cells (stateless clusters): one cell at a time is drained from the traffic layer,
%% changed (cluster upgrade, rebuild or application release), verified and put back. Same pipeline in dev, acc, prd.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Pipeline<br/>(cluster upgrade or release)
    participant T as Traffic layer / cell router<br/>(Front Door / App Gateway)
    participant A as Cell aks-env-sl-az1
    participant B as Cell aks-env-sl-az2
    Note over A,B: Both cells serve, users pinned by cell affinity, each cell can carry 100 % (N+1)
    P->>B: Pre-scale: raise HPA minReplicas / node count to full-load capacity
    P->>T: Take az1 out (disable origin / remove from backend pool)
    T-->>A: Connection draining – pinned users move to az2 (old version)
    P->>A: Upgrade control plane + node pools (or rebuild from IaC)<br/>or move the cell's release tag
    A->>A: Flux reconciles all apps, health checks
    P->>A: Smoke + synthetic tests through the per-cell test host names
    P->>T: Return az1 (Front Door weights 10 % → 50 % → 100 %) – only new sessions land there
    Note over P: Watch error rate / latency SLO. Breach → take az1 out again, stop (release: revert tag).
    P->>A: Soak, pre-scale az1, then repeat steps 2–7 for az2 (and az3): its users move to az1 once
    P->>B: Remove pre-scale, autoscalers take over
